IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-parental`
IMPORT `ei1-seat`

-- Worked cases for ei1-seat.l4 (Employment Insurance Act, Part I, ss 6 to 23.3(5)): at least one case for every question of the seat,
-- written the way a person in the seat would answer, with the expected value worked out by hand from the text of the section named
-- beside the case (never copied from the encoding's own output). Dates and week counts were worked out with a calendar program that is
-- not the encoding. A question whose input a case does not mention gets the neutral answer: no, 0, or 2026-01-04, so read each case with
-- the question's inputs in mind. Cases that end in NOTHING are the explicit "not covered" cases: the text gives the question no answer
-- (a violation for which only a warning was imposed has no class, s 7.1(5); the regular maximum is not in s 12(3); no claim under both
-- Parts; a benefit period before 1997 has no maximum weekly insurable earnings, s 14(1.1)). One #ASSERT per line.


§ `s 6 -- attachment claimants and suitable employment (src:141-142, 150-155)`
-- s 6(1) "disentitled": not entitled under section 13.
#ASSERT `Am I disentitled from receiving benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Or under section 50.
#ASSERT `Am I disentitled from receiving benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Or under the regulations.
#ASSERT `Am I disentitled from receiving benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I disentitled from receiving benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1) "disqualified": under section 27 or 30.
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified from receiving benefits` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified from receiving benefits` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I disqualified from receiving benefits` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1) "initial claim for benefits".
#ASSERT `Is my claim an initial claim for benefits` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my claim an initial claim for benefits` FALSE)
-- 600 or more hours: major (s 6(1)).
#ASSERT `Am I a major attachment claimant` TRUE 600
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a major attachment claimant` TRUE 599)
-- A claimant who does not qualify is neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a major attachment claimant` FALSE 700)
-- Fewer than 600 hours: minor.
#ASSERT `Am I a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 599
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 600)
-- s 6(4)(a): work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute.
#ASSERT `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(4)(b): usual occupation, lower rate than the agreement.
#ASSERT `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(4)(b): no agreement, so good employers' conditions are the benchmark.
#ASSERT `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- With an agreement, what good employers recognize is not the benchmark.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(4)(c): not in my usual occupation, lower rate than I might reasonably expect.
#ASSERT `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(5): after a reasonable interval (c) stops applying if the job is no worse than the benchmark.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 6(5) does not help if the job is below the benchmark.
#ASSERT `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Nothing wrong with the job.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

